{"problem": "all_rotations\n\nYield the circular shifts of *iterable*.\n\n>>> list(all_rotations(range(4)))\n[(0, 1, 2, 3), (1, 2, 3, 0), (2, 3, 0, 1), (3, 0, 1, 2)]\n\nSet *steps* to the number of places to rotate to the left\n(or to the right if negative).  Defaults to 1.\n\n>>> list(all_rotations(range(4), 2))\n[(0, 1, 2, 3), (2, 3, 0, 1)]\n\n>>> list(all_rotations(range(4), -1))\n[(0, 1, 2, 3), (3, 0, 1, 2), (2, 3, 0, 1), (1, 2, 3, 0)]", "resolution": "def all_rotations(iterable, steps=1):\n    \"\"\"Yield the circular shifts of *iterable*.\n\n    >>> list(all_rotations(range(4)))\n    [(0, 1, 2, 3), (1, 2, 3, 0), (2, 3, 0, 1), (3, 0, 1, 2)]\n\n    Set *steps* to the number of places to rotate to the left\n    (or to the right if negative).  Defaults to 1.\n\n    >>> list(all_rotations(range(4), 2))\n    [(0, 1, 2, 3), (2, 3, 0, 1)]\n\n    >>> list(all_rotations(range(4), -1))\n    [(0, 1, 2, 3), (3, 0, 1, 2), (2, 3, 0, 1), (1, 2, 3, 0)]\n\n    \"\"\"\n    buffer = deque(iterable)\n    if steps == 0:\n        raise ValueError('Steps should be a non-zero integer')\n\n    buffer.rotate(steps)\n    steps = -steps\n    n = len(buffer)\n    n //= math.gcd(n, steps)\n\n    for _ in repeat(None, n):\n        buffer.rotate(steps)\n        yield tuple(buffer)\n", "text": "all_rotations"}